#COLLECTION
CO:COLLECTION_SUMMARY            	INS-1 (832/13) cells (#SCC207, Sigma-Aldrich) were cultured as monolayers in
CO:COLLECTION_SUMMARY            	RPMI 1640 medium (#11875, Gibco™) supplemented with 10% (v/v) fetal bovine
CO:COLLECTION_SUMMARY            	serum (#16140-071, Gibco™), antibiotics (10,000 units/mL penicillin and 10
CO:COLLECTION_SUMMARY            	mg/mL streptomycin) (#15140122, Gibco™), 10mM HEPES (#15630-080, Gibco™), 2
CO:COLLECTION_SUMMARY            	mM L-glutamine (#35050-061, Gibco™), 1 mM sodium pyruvate (#11360-070,
CO:COLLECTION_SUMMARY            	Gibco™), and 50 µM β-mercaptoethanol (BME) (#M6250, Sigma-Aldrich).
CO:SAMPLE_TYPE                   	INS-1 cells
#TREATMENT
TR:TREATMENT_SUMMARY             	INS-1 cells (~2.5 million cells per dish) were seeded into 100 mm tissue
TR:TREATMENT_SUMMARY             	culture-treated dishes (#0877222, Corning). After overnight incubation, +BME
TR:TREATMENT_SUMMARY             	medium was aspirated and replaced with 10 mL of experimental medium (-BME or
TR:TREATMENT_SUMMARY             	-BME+BSO medium) for 24 hours. Prior to metabolite extraction, treated cells
TR:TREATMENT_SUMMARY             	underwent a glucose-stimulated insulin secretion assay (2.5mM glucose).
#SAMPLEPREP
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	For extraction, cells were washed 2x with 1 mL cold DBPS to remove culture
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	medium and scrapped from the dish in 1 mL ice-cold acetonitrile:methanol:water
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	(2:2:1 %v/v/v) and transferred to 1.5 mL centrifuge tubes. Cells were lysed
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	through three snap-freeze thaw cycles, following centrifugation at 15,000 RPM
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	for 10 minutes at 4ºC. The supernatants containing soluble metabolites were
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	transferred to clean 1.5 mL centrifuge tubes and evaporated in a vacuum
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	concentrator (SPD111V#, Savant) The remaining pellets were processed for total
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	protein quantification using the Pierce BCA Protein Assay Kit (Thermo Fisher
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	Scientific). Dry extracts were reconstituted in 100 μL acetonitrile:water (1:1,
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	%v/v) containing 10 μL of IROA Internal Standard U-13C, 95% (IROA® TrueQuant
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	IQQ Kit, IROA Technologies™) and centrifuged (10,000 RPM) for 10 minutes at
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	4°C (to remove insoluble debris). One hundred μL of the supernatant was
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	transferred into liquid chromatography-mass spectrometry vials (TrueView LC–MS
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	Certified, Waters Corporation) for liquid chromatography-mass spectrometry
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	analysis. Quality Control (QC) samples: 80 μL of the sample supernatant was
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	removed before the evaporation step. The aliquots were all pooled, sample volume
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	matched, and aliquots were evaporated to dryness, stored, and reconstituted as
SP:SAMPLEPREP_SUMMARY            	described above.
#CHROMATOGRAPHY
CH:CHROMATOGRAPHY_TYPE           	HILIC
CH:INSTRUMENT_NAME               	Waters Acquity I-Class
CH:COLUMN_NAME                   	Waters ACQUITY UPLC BEH Amide (100 x 2.1mm,1.7um)
CH:SOLVENT_A                     	100% water; 25 mM ammonium hydroxide; 25 mM ammonium acetate
CH:SOLVENT_B                     	100% acetonitrile
CH:FLOW_GRADIENT                 	95% B (0–0.5 min), 95%-65% B (0.5–7 min), 65–40% B (7–8 min), 40% B
CH:FLOW_GRADIENT                 	(8–9 min), 40–95% B (9–9.1 min) and continuing at 95% B (9.1–12.0 min)
CH:FLOW_RATE                     	0.5mL/min
CH:COLUMN_TEMPERATURE            	30
#ANALYSIS
AN:ANALYSIS_TYPE                 	MS
#MS
MS:INSTRUMENT_NAME               	Waters Xevo-G2-XS
MS:INSTRUMENT_TYPE               	QTOF
MS:MS_TYPE                       	ESI
MS:ION_MODE                      	NEGATIVE
MS:MS_COMMENTS                   	Q-ToF–MS scan data (300 ms/scan; mass scan range 50–1200 Da) were first
MS:MS_COMMENTS                   	acquired for each sample. Thereafter, MSe fragmentation data were acquired for
MS:MS_COMMENTS                   	metabolite identification (low energy scan: 200 ms/scan, collision energy 6 eV;
MS:MS_COMMENTS                   	high energy scan: 100 ms/scan, collision energy 10, 20, 30 and 40 eV, mass scan
MS:MS_COMMENTS                   	range 25–1000 Da). ESI source parameters were as follows: 1.8 kV capillary
MS:MS_COMMENTS                   	voltage, 40 V sampling cone, 50°C source temperature, 420°C desolvation
MS:MS_COMMENTS                   	temperature, 80 L/hr cone gas flow, 850 L/hr desolvation gas flow
